From: HackerOS Linux System <hackeros068@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 30/35] hackeros: perf events bez uprawnien dla red team side-channel

Konfiguruje perf_event_paranoid na wartosc umozliwiajaca red team
side-channel research (Spectre/Meltdown analysis, cache-timing
attacks, DRAM rowhammer timing) bez pelnego roota. Dostepne dla
grupy hackeros-redteam z pelnym audytem.

---
 kernel/events/core.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/kernel/events/core.c
+++ b/kernel/events/core.c
@@ -440,6 +440,26 @@
 int sysctl_perf_event_sample_rate	__read_mostly	= DEFAULT_MAX_SAMPLE_RATE;
 static int max_samples_per_tick		__read_mostly	= DIV_ROUND_UP(DEFAULT_MAX_SAMPLE_RATE, HZ);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_HACKEROS_REDTEAM
+/*
+ * HackerOS Red Team: rozszerzone perf events dla side-channel research.
+ *
+ * hackeros_perf_redteam_paranoid: ustawienie perf_event_paranoid
+ * efektywne dla procesow z grupy hackeros-redteam. Domyslnie -1
+ * (pelny dostep do wszystkich hardware counters), umozliwiajac:
+ * - PMU counter analysis dla Spectre gadget research
+ * - cache-timing attacks (Flush+Reload, Prime+Probe)
+ * - DRAM timing analysis (Rowhammer research)
+ * - CPU branch predictor analysis
+ *
+ * System globalny perf_event_paranoid pozostaje niezmieniony (=3
+ * ustawione przez patch 0010), wiec to jest targeted exemption
+ * tylko dla grupy red team, nie globalne obnizenie bezpieczenstwa.
+ */
+static int hackeros_perf_redteam_paranoid __read_mostly = -1;
+static const int hackeros_perf_redteam_present = 1;
+#endif /* CONFIG_HACKEROS_REDTEAM */
--
